+ * Blood Wake carried patch (D-016 Remastered surround, docs/day1/D2.md part
+ * 3): the source voice carries 6 channels (5.1: FL FR FC LFE BL BR) when
+ * bw_surround_output_wanted() says so for the device found; otherwise it is
+ * as before (2 channels into a 2-channel mastering voice). And (0.2.5 item
+ * 68) a lost or changed audio device is rebuilt on the default one: see
+ * xa2_check_device. And (lat-a; every edition's default since 0.3.0, lane
+ * au-orig) the same contract can run on a WASAPI shared-mode stream instead
+ * of XAudio2 (bw_apu_wasapi.c): see "Two outputs" below. And (au-out, the
+ * audio rework's output lane, docs/audio/out.md) a lost or changed device is
+ * opened on a worker and swapped in at a period boundary (every edition,
+ * call AO-3; BW_AUDIO_REBUILD_WORKER), each open names its device in one line ("[XA2]
+ * output device:"), and the WASAPI output is event-driven with its pacing
+ * marks in samples (xa2_wait_event, xa2_marks_samples). The original file is
+ * xboxrecomp/src/apu/apu_xaudio2.c (sha256 guarded in CMakeLists.txt).
