+ *
+ * BW_LATLOG (src/bw_latlog.c) also gets, from here: each device buffer
+ * submitted (B: the WAV index of its first sample, the buffers queued before,
+ * the samples played then), each XAudio2 processing pass of the source voice
+ * (J: the bytes it still needed, the samples played), and about once a second
+ * XAudio2's own performance data (K: CurrentLatencyInSamples, its glitch
+ * count). At init it reads (never changes) the default device's periods.
