+ * bw_wa_wanted: every edition by default since 0.3.0; BW_AUDIO_OUT=xaudio2
+ * keeps XAudio2) instead of an XAudio2 source voice. Everything above the device stays the
+ * same: the pacing reads the queue (here the stream's padding: frames written
+ * and not yet read by Windows' engine, exact), each period is written as it
+ * is made (no 512-sample staging), the rebuild on a lost or changed device,
+ * the wait while there is none, BW_TEST_AUDIO_LOST and BW_AUDIO_REBUILD, the
+ * underrun count and the played count. If the stream can't be opened at boot
+ * for any reason but "no device", the boot falls back to XAudio2.
+ *
+ * Short passes (BW_XA2_STATS / BW_LATLOG, both outputs): either engine reads
+ * 480 frames a pass at 48 kHz (XAudio2's quantum, and the shared engine's
+ * period on this PC), so the played count moves in whole passes; a move that
