+/* ---- Blood Wake (au-out): the top-up just in time (BW_WASAPI_LEAD) -------
+ *
+ * Event-driven, the stream is topped up right after each pass: the next pass
+ * is 10 ms away, so the samples written then wait about a period before the
+ * engine reads them. BW_WASAPI_LEAD=<ms> (wherever the WASAPI output runs;
+ * off unless set, never in a preset) tops it up that long before the next pass instead, from the
+ * passes' own times (each wake on the engine's event after a wait). The
+ * samples are then that much younger when read; the lead must cover making a
+ * pass's worth of periods (the DSP stage's share above all) plus the
+ * scheduler's delay. A late top-up is a short pass, counted. The slack of
+ * each critical write (the one that brings the queue up to a whole pass) to
+ * the next pass is counted for BW_XA2_STATS in either mode. */
+static int64_t g_pass_us;              /* the last pass seen (a wake on the event after a wait) */
+static int64_t g_lead_us = -1;
